<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Henri Rivière</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1827">1827</a>–<a href="/years/1883">1883</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Henri Rivière was a French naval officer and writer. Sent to Tonkin in 1882, he seized the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hanoi">Hanoi</a> citadel in April of that year, provoking a crisis with the Vietnamese court and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>. He was killed by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-flag-army">Black Flag Army</a> at the Battle of Paper Bridge near Hanoi on 19 May 1883, and his death led <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> to send reinforcements and impose a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">protectorate</a> on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a>.</p></div>
